 ## Shared principles
-All domain manipulation operators follow a common convention: the input position vector $\mathbf{p}$ is passed as the first argument and modified in place (`inout p`) [S1, S2, unofficial]. For operators acting on subsets of dimensions, specific components are supplied (e.g., `<p.x>` or `<p.zx>`) [S1, unofficial].
